--- Rosetta Code: Averages/Mean angle
--- https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Averages/Mean_angle
--- Each angle is a point on the unit circle; the mean angle is the direction of
--- their sum, atan2 of the sines' sum and the cosines' sum, back in degrees.
--- (atan2 is element-wise over tensors, so the two sums go in as one-item lists.)

use math

--- the mean of angles given in degrees, in degrees
fn mean_angle[degrees]
    radians = tensor[degrees] * pi / 180
    direction = atan2[[sum[sin[radians]]], [sum[cos[radians]]]]
    return direction[0] * 180 / pi

--- lists of different lengths: a nested literal of numbers would be a matrix
samples = []
samples = push[samples, [350, 10]]
samples = push[samples, [90, 180, 270, 360]]
samples = push[samples, [10, 20, 30]]
for angles in samples
    log['The mean angle of `angles` is `fmt[mean_angle[angles], decimals = 4]` degrees']
